  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The manganese heptoxide&nbsp;solubility properties indicate that it is a&nbsp;nonpolar molecular species, which is confirmed by its structure. The molecules consist of a pair of tetrahedra that share a common vertex. The vertices are occupied by oxygen atoms and at the centres of the tetrahedra are the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math> centres. The connectivity is indicated by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>Mn</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e0d9a2a4-c6dc-4ae7-9338-f51da5b847cd-image.png\" style=\"width: 194px; height: 100px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
